      "text": "Given the relationship between pressure (\\(P\\)) and volume (\\(V\\)) at constant temperature, we have:\n\n\\[\nP \\propto \\frac{1}{V}\n\\]\n\nThis can be written as:\n\n\\[\nP_1 V_1 = P_2 V_2\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(P_1\\) and \\(V_1\\) are the initial pressure and volume, and \\(P_2\\) and \\(V_2\\) are the final pressure and volume.\n\nGiven:\n\\[\nP_1 = 5 \\text{ kPa}, \\quad V_1 = 2.28 \\text{ liters}, \\quad V_2 = 5.7 \\text{ liters}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(P_2\\). Using the relationship:\n\n\\[\nP_1 V_1 = P_2 V_2\n\\]\n\nSubstitute the given values:\n\n\\[\n5 \\text{ kPa} \\times 2.28 \\text{ liters} = P_2 \\times 5.7 \\text{ liters}\n\\]\n\nCalculate the left-hand side:\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 2.28 = 11.4 \\text{ kPa} \\cdot \\text{liters}\n\\]\n\nNow solve for \\(P_2\\):\n\n\\[\n11.4 \\text{ kPa} \\cdot \\text{liters} = P_2 \\times 5.7 \\text{ liters}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nP_2 = \\frac{11.4 \\text{ kPa} \\cdot \\text{liters}}{5.7 \\text{ liters}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nP_2 = 2 \\text{ kPa}\n\\]\n\nThus, the new pressure when the oxygen is moved to a 5.7 liter container is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2 \\text{ kPa}}\n\\]",
